+        <ul class="slist">
+          <li><svg class="ico"><use href="#i-check"/></svg><span><b>It says the category out loud.</b> Every other candidate talked around longevity. This one puts age on the door and then overturns it, which is a more confident move than avoiding the word.</span></li>
+          <li><svg class="ico"><use href="#i-check"/></svg><span><b>The identity is pre-solved.</b> The mark is the name rotated. One gesture generates the logo, the animation, the pattern and the merch. Very few names arrive with their visual system already inside them.</span></li>
+          <li><svg class="ico"><use href="#i-check"/></svg><span><b>Four characters.</b> Reads at any size, fits any handle, survives a favicon, and types in one second. Operationally the lightest name in the whole process.</span></li>
+          <li><svg class="ico"><use href="#i-check"/></svg><span><b>The register and the domains are smiling.</b> No identical mark in sight on TMview and nine extensions open at pocket money prices. After the ReFrame reading, that is not a small argument.</span></li>
+          <li><svg class="ico"><use href="#i-check"/></svg><span><b>No translation problem.</b> Age is understood in Romanian without being Romanian, and the numeral is universal. It travels as far as the franchise ambition does.</span></li>
